COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AC157276.2 and X60703.1.
            
            On May 4, 2006 this sequence version replaced XP_980277.1.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a membrane-bound glycoprotein. The
            encoded enzyme plays a central role in thyroid gland function. The
            enzyme functions in the iodination of tyrosine residues in
            thyroglobulin and phenoxy-ester formation between pairs of
            iodinated tyrosines to generate the thyroid hormones, thyroxine and
            triiodothyronine. Mice with homozygous missense mutations in this
            gene exhibit hypothyroid dwarfism and hearing impairment. [provided
            by RefSeq, Sep 2015].
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
